ms. For those, we should be able to report a character index range instead. And even for some rules that look for structural problems, often only a portion of that node is responsible for the actual error. For instance, when reporting on an improperly wrapped IIFE, the entire CallExpression is reported instead of just the location of the misplaced `)`. @nzakas: Do you think we should allow `context.report` to accept a range and make the `node` optional?\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/comments/38843598/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"michaelficarra","id":218840,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxODg0MA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/218840?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelficarra","html_url":"https://github.com/michaelficarra","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelficarra/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelficarra/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelficarra/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelficarra/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelficarra/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelficarra/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelficarra/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelficarra/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelficarra/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":106186887,"node_id":"MDE0Ok1lbnRpb25lZEV2ZW50MTA2MTg2ODg3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/events/106186887","actor":{"login":"nzakas","id":38546,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NTQ2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubuserconten